    "original_author": "",
    "original_author_id": 0,
    "body": "> Host machine Node is too indeterministic. I think bundling is the only realistic option to have a guaranteed working and compatible node version. GitHub currently runs all actions on Node 24, and I think next version will be 27.\n> \n> Only by running the exact same version we can guarantee maximum compatibility.\n\nIt would be great if we could stay aligned with GitHub; at the very least, this would allow us to manually replace the Node 24 version located in the `externals` directory (or whatever we might choose to call it). Since our system still needs to run on CentOS 7, we compile Node 24 ourselves.",
